{"id": "8cfebb11-6f73-4577-923a-dfbca8b61ef3", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This matches the 400 BadRequestException pattern: MediaTailor sessions have a finite lifetime, so a long pause causes the session and its manifest ID to expire server-side. When playback resumes with the stale session ID still embedded in the URL, MediaTailor rejects it as invalid, producing the 400 error.

The fix is for the player to detect this and reinitialize the session (calling the session initialization endpoint again for a fresh ID) rather than resuming with the stale one, essentially treating a long pause like a fresh launch.

"}]}
